081 verify-shared-kv-cuda-sinks: grouped (GQA) target verify for DFlash on CUDA

Opt-in via SGLANG_VERIFY_SHARED_KV_CUDA=1. The speculative target verify (topk 1,
decode attention mode) runs upstream's shared-KV grouped kernel on CUDA instead of
the per-head split-KV kernel on global-attention layers: one pass over each KV
head serves all of its query heads. Adds what the upstream kernel lacked for
Flint: learned attention sinks in the stage-2 LSE merge and a compute-dtype
upcast for fp8 KV. SWA layers and MLA keep the per-head path.
Flint DFlash2 natural-text decode 105 -> 126 tok/s at 131K, 82 -> 116 at 262K.
